        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="callout callout--gold">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      Do not pick a first job by base pay alone. An agency role that gives you real pitch ownership at
      Rs 3 LPA can build a stronger portfolio, and get you to Rs 8-10 LPA faster, than a quieter in-house
      role at Rs 5 LPA where you rarely touch media directly for the first two years.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="salary-by-city">Pay by city and agency type</h2>
  <p>
    Where you work matters almost as much as how long you have worked. Mumbai and Delhi-NCR remain the
    two largest PR hubs in India, largely because most major agencies keep their head offices and
    strongest media relationships there.
