  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>
  <p>
    Do not spend another month reading generic "how to get into PR" advice without producing anything.
    Decide this week whether agency or in-house fits your current stage better, then write one real press
    release and one real pitch before you send a single application — that single piece of proof does more
    for your first interview than another certificate.
  </p>
  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--gold">
    <p>Run yourself through The 4-Checkpoint Protocol above, honestly, on paper.</p>
    <p>Then start Gate 1: write one real, defensible press release and pitch before you apply anywhere.</p>
  </div>
  <p>
    Building toward earlier financial freedom through a career in public relations comes down to a genuine
